#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""arr-mismatch: READ-ONLY nightly check for Radarr library files that are probably the wrong movie.

Why (report ~/reports/unraid/indexer-misid-2026-10-13.md): some indexers stamp the searched TMDB/IMDb ID onto
unrelated releases, and Radarr's import guard compares titles but not years. That is how Night Shift (2001) landed
as Night Shift (2017), Glass Tower (1987) as Glass Tower II (2010) and Die stille Bucht (1988) as
Quiet Bay (2026).

  arr-mismatch [list | --dry-run]   scan now and print the current suspects (changes nothing, state untouched)
  arr-mismatch --cron               scan; ONE ~/inbox note listing suspects not seen before; silent otherwise
  arr-mismatch ack KEY...           mark suspects as known (no alert), e.g. ack radarr:1234 (owner said "fine",
                                    or he is being asked about it anyway)
  arr-mismatch --status             state summary
  add --json to list for machine-readable output.

  arr-mismatch grabs [--since MIN] [--json]
                                    GRAB-TIME check, dry run: Radarr queue items + grabs of the last MIN minutes
                                    (default 40) whose release name is another movie; prints all, changes nothing
  arr-mismatch grabs --cron         the same every 15 min, deduped by downloadId (~/.local/state/arr-mismatch-grabs.json),
                                    and AUTO-DROPS each clear mismatch:
                                      1. still in the queue: DELETE /api/v3/queue/ID?removeFromClient&blocklist&skipRedownload
                                      2. left the queue, not imported: POST /api/v3/history/failed/ID (= blocklist)
                                         already imported (queue state importing/imported, or an import event for the
                                         downloadId): never touched, ONE ~/inbox note (library files are
                                         never deleted; the nightly library check flags the file)
                                      3. regrab: interactive search GET /api/v3/release?movieId=, the best APPROVED
                                         release (Radarr's order) whose parsed name carries a known title of the movie
                                         and a year within +-1 (grab_check, or TMDB re-dating) -> POST /api/v3/release;
                                         none -> the movie stays missing (said in the note); skipped when Radarr
                                         already has another download queued for the movie
                                      caps: 3 auto-drops per movie per 7 days (then a note "indexer keeps mis-IDing"),
                                      10 per run (then notes). Every action -> ~/.local/state/arr-mismatch-drops.log;
                                      ONE ~/inbox note per run that dropped something. Never messages the owner itself.
                                    Kill switch: --no-drop, or the file ~/.config/arr-mismatch/no-drop -> notes only
                                    (ONE note per mismatched release with the exact drop + search command).
  arr-mismatch drop MOVIEID queue:ID | history:ID [--dry-run]
                                    owner-approved drop of ONE grab (the command those notes print): the auto-drop's
                                    write (1. or 2. above), then Radarr's own search for the movie (MoviesSearch);
                                    logged to ~/.local/state/arr-mismatch-drops.log
  arr-mismatch grabs --cron --dry-run
                                    the cron run without any write: prints what it would drop / regrab (it does run
                                    the interactive search, GET), no notes, state untouched
  arr-mismatch grabs --status       grab-check state summary (+ auto-drops of the last 7 days, kill switch)

Grab-time rule (no file yet, so no runtime): the release title, parsed by /api/v3/parse, must carry the movie's
title / original / alternate title AND a year within +-1 of the movie's year. A CLEAR mismatch (note) is:
  - the parsed year is off by more than 1 (more than 2 when the name carries the movie's main/original title: Long
    Road TCC 2006/2011; an alternate title cannot clear it: Quiet Bay; nor a main title 3+ years off: a
    same-title remake like Steel Sentinel 1987/2014); exemption for TMDB re-dating (Stage Story 2020 -> 2025): the name
    carries the MAIN/original title and its year is within +-1 of one of the movie's release dates (in cinemas /
    digital / physical), or
  - the title is not a known title of the movie AND the parser maps the name to ANOTHER movie in the library, or
    the name shares not one significant word with any of the movie's titles (Bright Morrow 2026 -> Masters
    of the Universe 2026; 6-month backtest: 13 hits, ~1 doubtful).
Backtest on 6 months of grabs (1,688): 47 flagged, ~45 really wrong (the report counted 54 by hand).
An unknown title alone (foreign names missing from TMDB's alternate titles) or a name without a year is not clear.

Per movie with a file, three signals:
  year     the release name (sceneName, else originalFilePath folder/file, else relativePath), parsed by Radarr's
           own GET /api/v3/parse, vs the movie's year / secondary year: disagrees when off by more than 1
  title    the parsed title(s) vs the movie's title, original title and alternate titles (normalized), or the
           parser maps the name to this movie: disagrees when none matches
  runtime  mediaInfo runTime vs the movie's runtime: disagrees when off by > 20% AND > 15 min
           (a longer file with an edition in the name, e.g. Director's Cut / Extended / Uncut: > 50% AND > 30 min)
Suspect when >= 2 signals disagree, or the year is off by >= 3 (a title and runtime match cannot clear that:
Quiet Bay and Glass Tower matched by alternate title and runtime). One exemption, for TMDB re-dating
(Stage Story 2020 -> 2025): only the year disagrees, the name carries the main/original title (an alternate title is
not enough) and the runtime is equal within 3 min / 3%.
Missing data (no year in the name, runtime 0) is "unknown", never a disagreement.

Radarr only: Sonarr matches by title/alias (report: 0 real mismatches in 3,728 grabs), and episode names carry
no year, so the same check there would be mostly noise.

Read-only except `grabs --cron` auto-drop (above): GET requests only (movie list / movie, parse; grabs: queue, grab
history). The API helper (api,
ApiError, norm, q) is shared with ~/bin/arr-unblock (loaded as a module): the Radarr URL from the profile
(services.radarr_url), the key by handle through core.egress; never printed (the note's drop command is
`arr-mismatch drop`, no key file).
State: ~/.local/state/arr-mismatch.json (known suspects, by radarr:<movieFileId>, so a replaced file is checked
afresh). Grabs: ~/.local/state/arr-mismatch-grabs.json (checked downloadIds, 30 days).
Grabs state also keeps "drops" ({movieId: [times]}, for the per-movie cap). The list/ack state is unchanged.
Env (tests): ARR_MISMATCH_STATE, ARR_MISMATCH_GRABS_STATE, ARR_MISMATCH_INBOX, ARR_MISMATCH_NO_DROP,
ARR_MISMATCH_DROPS_LOG.
Exit: 0 ok (list / grabs dry run: 3 when there are suspects), 1 error.
"""
import argparse, importlib.machinery, importlib.util, json, os, re, sys, time
from datetime import datetime

sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
_ldr = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("arr_unblock", os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)),
                                                                        "arr-unblock"))
AU = importlib.util.module_from_spec(importlib.util.spec_from_loader("arr_unblock", _ldr))
_ldr.exec_module(AU)
api, ApiError, norm, q = AU.api, AU.ApiError, AU.norm, AU.q

STATE = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("ARR_MISMATCH_STATE") or "~/.local/state/arr-mismatch.json")
INBOX = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("ARR_MISMATCH_INBOX") or "~/inbox")
YEAR_TOL = 1          # +-1: TMDB vs release-name year
YEAR_HARD = 3         # off by this much -> suspect on its own
RT_PCT, RT_MIN = 0.20, 15
ED_PCT, ED_MIN = 0.50, 30   # longer file + an edition in the name (Director's Cut, Extended, Uncut)
SAME_PCT, SAME_MIN = 0.03, 3  # runtime "to the minute" for the re-dated exemption
FAIL_NOTE = 2         # consecutive failed cron runs before one note
GRABS_STATE = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("ARR_MISMATCH_GRABS_STATE")
                                 or "~/.local/state/arr-mismatch-grabs.json")
GRAB_WINDOW = 40      # minutes of grab history per run (cron */15; the overlap is deduped by downloadId)
GRAB_KEEP_DAYS = 30   # forget checked downloadIds after this long (unless still in the queue)
GRAB_FAIL_NOTE = 8    # consecutive failed */15 runs (~2 h) before one note (arr-unblock already notes outages)
# auto-drop
NO_DROP_FILE = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("ARR_MISMATCH_NO_DROP") or "~/.config/arr-mismatch/no-drop")
DROPS_LOG = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get("ARR_MISMATCH_DROPS_LOG") or "~/.local/state/arr-mismatch-drops.log")
DROP_CAP, DROP_CAP_DAYS = 3, 7   # auto-drops per movie per 7 days; after that a note only ("indexer keeps mis-IDing")
DROP_RUN_MAX = 10                # auto-drops per run
REGRAB_TRY = 15                  # approved releases parsed at most when picking the replacement
SEARCH_TIMEOUT = 150             # s, interactive release search (GET /api/v3/release asks every indexer)
IMPORT_EVENTS = {"downloadFolderImported", "movieFolderImported", "3"}


# ---------- pure logic (unit-tested) ----------

def minutes(rt):
    """mediaInfo runTime "1:57:03" / "57:03" -> minutes (float); None when missing or zero."""
    parts = str(rt or "").strip().split(":")
    try:
        nums = [float(p) for p in parts]
    except ValueError:
        return None
    if not nums or len(nums) > 3:
        return None
    while len(nums) < 3:
        nums.insert(0, 0.0)
    m = nums[0] * 60 + nums[1] + nums[2] / 60
    return m or None


def names(mf):
    """Release names to parse, best first: sceneName, originalFilePath folder + file, relativePath file."""
    out = []
    def add(s):
        s = (s or "").strip()
        s = re.sub(r"\.[A-Za-z0-9]{2,4}$", "", s) if re.search(r"\.(mkv|mp4|m4v|avi|ts|m2ts|wmv|mov|webm|mpe?g)$",
                                                               s, re.I) else s
        if s and s not in out:
            out.append(s)
    add(mf.get("sceneName"))
    op = (mf.get("originalFilePath") or "").replace("\\", "/")
    if op:
        parts = [p for p in op.split("/") if p]
        if len(parts) > 1:
            add(parts[-2])
        add(parts[-1] if parts else "")
    rp = (mf.get("relativePath") or "").replace("\\", "/")
    add(rp.split("/")[-1])
    return out


def pick(parsed):
    """parsed: list of (name, parse result). First name with a year wins, else the first with a title."""
    best = None
    for name, p in parsed:
        pm = (p or {}).get("parsedMovieInfo") or {}
        titles = [t for t in (pm.get("movieTitles") or [pm.get("movieTitle")]) if t]
        rec = {"name": name, "titles": titles, "year": pm.get("year") or None, "edition": pm.get("edition") or "",
               "mapped": ((p or {}).get("movie") or {}).get("id")}
        if rec["year"]:
            return rec
        if titles and best is None:
            best = rec
    return best


def check(movie, rel):
    """Signals for one movie + its picked release info. Returns dict with year/title/runtime verdicts
    (True = disagrees, False = agrees, None = unknown), year_off, file/movie minutes and suspect flag."""
    mf = movie.get("movieFile") or {}
    r = {"year": None, "title": None, "runtime": None, "year_off": None}
    if rel and rel.get("year"):
        years = [y for y in (movie.get("year"), movie.get("secondaryYear")) if y]
        if years:
            r["year_off"] = min(abs(rel["year"] - y) for y in years)
            r["year"] = r["year_off"] > YEAR_TOL
    main_title = False
    if rel and rel.get("titles"):
        mains = {norm(movie.get("title")), norm(movie.get("originalTitle"))}
        known = mains | {norm(a.get("title")) for a in movie.get("alternateTitles") or []}
        known.discard(""), mains.discard("")
        parsed = {norm(t) for t in rel["titles"]}
        main_title = bool(parsed & mains)
        r["title"] = not (parsed & known or (rel.get("mapped") and rel["mapped"] == movie.get("id")))
    fm, mm = minutes((mf.get("mediaInfo") or {}).get("runTime")), movie.get("runtime") or None
    r["file_min"], r["movie_min"] = (round(fm) if fm else None), mm
    if fm and mm:
        d = abs(fm - mm)
        pct, mins = RT_PCT, RT_MIN
        if fm > mm and (rel or {}).get("edition") or fm > mm and mf.get("edition"):
            pct, mins = ED_PCT, ED_MIN      # Director's Cut / Extended / Uncut run longer
        r["runtime"] = d > mins and d > pct * mm
    bad = [k for k in ("year", "title", "runtime") if r[k]]
    r["bad"] = bad
    hard = (r["year_off"] or 0) >= YEAR_HARD
    # TMDB re-dated the film (Stage Story 2020 -> 2025): only the year disagrees, the name carries the movie's own
    # main/original title (not just an alternate one) and the runtime matches to the minute -> same film
    r["redated"] = bool(hard and bad == ["year"] and main_title and fm and mm
                        and abs(fm - mm) <= max(SAME_MIN, SAME_PCT * mm))
    r["suspect"] = (len(bad) >= 2 or hard) and not r["redated"]
    return r


def reason(movie, rel, r):
    bits = []
    if r["year"]:
        bits.append(f"year {rel['year']} vs {movie.get('year')}")
    if r["title"]:
        bits.append(f"title \"{' / '.join(rel['titles'])}\" not a known title")
    if r["runtime"]:
        bits.append(f"runtime {r['file_min']} vs {r['movie_min']} min")
    elif r["file_min"] and r["movie_min"]:
        bits.append(f"runtime ok ({r['file_min']} vs {r['movie_min']} min)")
    return "; ".join(bits)


# ---------- scan ----------

def parse(get, name):
    """GET /api/v3/parse for one name. A name without a year that fits two library movies (Red Door 2003 / 2013)
    makes Radarr answer HTTP 500 "Expected one movie, but found 2": that is "unknown", not an error."""
    try:
        return get("radarr", "GET", "/api/v3/parse?title=" + q(name))
    except ApiError as e:
        if "Expected one movie" in str(e) or "MultipleMoviesFound" in str(e):
            return None
        raise


def scan(get=None):
    """All Radarr movies with a file -> list of suspect dicts, plus the set of all current file keys.
    Read-only: GET /api/v3/movie and GET /api/v3/parse only."""
    get = get or api
    movies = get("radarr", "GET", "/api/v3/movie") or []
    out, keys = [], set()
    for m in movies:
        mf = m.get("movieFile")
        if not (m.get("hasFile") and mf and mf.get("id")):
            continue
        key = f"radarr:{mf['id']}"
        keys.add(key)
        parsed = []
        for n in names(mf):
            parsed.append((n, parse(get, n)))
            pm = (parsed[-1][1] or {}).get("parsedMovieInfo") or {}
            if pm.get("year"):
                break
        rel = pick(parsed)
        r = check(m, rel)
        if r["suspect"]:
            out.append({"key": key, "movieId": m.get("id"), "title": m.get("title"), "year": m.get("year"),
                        "name": (rel or {}).get("name"), "parsed_year": (rel or {}).get("year"),
                        "signals": r["bad"], "why": reason(m, rel, r), "size": mf.get("size") or 0,
                        "added": (mf.get("dateAdded") or "")[:10]})
    out.sort(key=lambda s: (s["title"] or "").lower())
    return out, keys


# ---------- state / output ----------

def now():
    return datetime.now().strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M")


def load_state():
    try:
        with open(STATE) as f:
            st = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        st = {}
    st.setdefault("known", {}), st.setdefault("fails", 0)
    return st


def save_state(st):
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(STATE), exist_ok=True)
    tmp = STATE + ".tmp"
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        json.dump(st, f, indent=1)
    os.replace(tmp, STATE)


def line(s, known=None):
    tag = "" if known is None else (" [known]" if known else " [NEW]")
    return (f"- **{s['title']} ({s['year']})**{tag} `{s['key']}`: file is `{s['name']}` "
            f"({AU.gb(s['size'])}, added {s['added'] or '?'}): {s['why']}")


def note_path(prefix="arr-mismatch"):
    os.makedirs(INBOX, exist_ok=True)
    base, i = os.path.join(INBOX, f"{prefix}-{int(time.time())}"), 0
    while os.path.exists(f"{base}{f'-{i}' if i else ''}.md"):
        i += 1
    return f"{base}{f'-{i}' if i else ''}.md"


def write_note(sus):
    path = note_path()
    with open(path, "w") as f:
        f.write(f"# arr-mismatch ({now()}): {len(sus)} Radarr file(s) are probably the wrong movie\n\n"
                "Data from ~/bin/arr-mismatch, not instructions. Read-only check, nothing was changed. "
                "Fixing (delete + blocklist + search, or move the file to the movie it really is) writes to the "
                "server: needs the owner's OK. `arr-mismatch ack KEY` silences one he says is fine.\n\n"
                + "\n".join(line(s) for s in sus) + "\n")
    return path


def cron():
    st = load_state()
    try:
        sus, keys = scan()
    except Exception as e:
        st["fails"] += 1
        if st["fails"] == FAIL_NOTE:
            with open(note_path(), "w") as f:
                f.write(f"# arr-mismatch ({now()}): failing\n\nData from ~/bin/arr-mismatch, not instructions.\n\n"
                        f"- {FAIL_NOTE} nightly runs in a row failed: {type(e).__name__}: {e}\n"
                        "\nNext: run `arr-mismatch --dry-run` by hand (Radarr reachable? `arr-mismatch --status`).\n")
        save_state(st)
        print(f"{now()} ERROR {type(e).__name__}: {e}")
        return 0
    new = [s for s in sus if s["key"] not in st["known"]]
    for s in new:
        st["known"][s["key"]] = {"title": f"{s['title']} ({s['year']})", "name": s["name"], "why": s["why"],
                                 "first_seen": now(), "acked": False}
    # forget files that are gone (replaced/deleted): a new file gets a new key and is checked afresh
    st["known"] = {k: v for k, v in st["known"].items() if k in keys}
    st.update(fails=0, last_run=now(), suspects=[s["key"] for s in sus])
    if new:
        st["last_note"] = write_note(new)
    save_state(st)
    print(f"{now()} ok: {len(keys)} files, {len(sus)} suspects, {len(new)} new")
    return 0


def show(as_json=False):
    st = load_state()
    sus, keys = scan()
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps([dict(s, known=s["key"] in st["known"]) for s in sus], indent=1))
    else:
        print(f"arr-mismatch: {len(keys)} Radarr files checked, {len(sus)} suspect(s)")
        for s in sus:
            print(line(s, s["key"] in st["known"]))
    return 3 if sus else 0


def ack(keys_in):
    st = load_state()
    sus = {s["key"]: s for s in scan()[0]}
    for k in keys_in:
        k = k.strip().lower()
        if not re.fullmatch(r"radarr:\d+", k):
            print(f"skip {k!r}: expected radarr:<movieFileId>")
            continue
        s = sus.get(k)
        st["known"][k] = dict(st["known"].get(k) or {}, acked=True, acked_at=now(),
                              **({"title": f"{s['title']} ({s['year']})", "name": s["name"], "why": s["why"]}
                                 if s else {}))
        print(f"known: {k}" + (f" {s['title']} ({s['year']})" if s else " (not a current suspect)"))
    save_state(st)
    return 0


def status():
    st = load_state()
    print(f"last run: {st.get('last_run') or 'never'}; current suspects: {len(st.get('suspects') or [])}; "
          f"known: {len(st['known'])}; consecutive failures: {st['fails']}")
    for k, v in sorted(st["known"].items()):
        print(f"- {k} {v.get('title', '')}{' (acked)' if v.get('acked') else ''}: {v.get('why', '')}")
    return 0


# ---------- grabs: grab-time check (queue + recent grab history) ----------

def date_years(movie):
    """Years of the movie's release dates (in cinemas, digital, physical, release date)."""
    out = set()
    for k in ("inCinemas", "digitalRelease", "physicalRelease", "releaseDate"):
        v = str(movie.get(k) or "")
        if re.match(r"\d{4}-", v):
            out.add(int(v[:4]))
    return out


FILLER = {"the", "and", "der", "die", "das", "und", "von", "auf", "for", "des", "del", "les", "with", "from", "ein",
          "eine", "part", "teil", "movie", "film", "into", "dem", "den", "una", "uno", "los", "las"}


def words(s):
    """Significant words of a title: accents folded, lowercase, >= 3 letters, no filler words or pure numbers."""
    s = AU.unicodedata.normalize("NFKD", str(s or ""))
    s = "".join(c for c in s if not AU.unicodedata.combining(c)).lower()
    return {w for w in re.split(r"[\W_]+", s) if len(w) >= 3 and not w.isdigit() and w not in FILLER}


def grab_check(movie, rel):
    """Grab-time verdict for one release name (pick() output) against the movie it was grabbed for. No file yet, so
    no runtime. Returns year/title verdicts (True = disagrees, False = agrees, None = unknown), year_off, other (the
    library movie id the parser maps the name to, when that is not this movie), redated and mismatch."""
    r = {"year": None, "title": None, "year_off": None, "other": None, "redated": False, "words": False,
         "mismatch": False}
    if not rel:
        return r
    mains = {norm(movie.get("title")), norm(movie.get("originalTitle"))}
    known = mains | {norm(a.get("title")) for a in movie.get("alternateTitles") or []}
    known.discard(""), mains.discard("")
    parsed = {norm(t) for t in rel.get("titles") or []} - {""}
    mapped = rel.get("mapped")
    if mapped and mapped != movie.get("id"):
        r["other"] = mapped
    main_title = bool(parsed & mains)
    if parsed:
        r["title"] = not (parsed & known or (mapped and mapped == movie.get("id")))
    if rel.get("year"):
        years = [y for y in (movie.get("year"), movie.get("secondaryYear")) if y]
        if years:
            r["year_off"] = min(abs(rel["year"] - y) for y in years)
            # the movie's own main/original title: +-2 (Long Road: The Complete Cut 2006 vs 2011/2004);
            # a same-title remake is further apart (Steel Sentinel 1987/2014, The Frost 1982/2011, Lone Unit 2016/2020)
            r["year"] = r["year_off"] > (YEAR_HARD - 1 if main_title else YEAR_TOL)
            # TMDB re-dated the film (Stage Story 2020 -> 2025): the main/original title + a year that fits one of the
            # movie's own release dates. An alternate title is not enough (Quiet Bay <- Die stille Bucht).
            if r["year"] and main_title and any(abs(rel["year"] - y) <= YEAR_TOL for y in date_years(movie)):
                r["year"], r["redated"] = False, True
    # same year, but the name shares not one significant word with any title of the movie (Bright Morrow /
    # Xing Guang Lu 2026 -> Sky Lords 2026): a foreign title would still share a name or a number word
    titles = [movie.get("title"), movie.get("originalTitle")] + [a.get("title")
                                                                 for a in movie.get("alternateTitles") or []]
    r["words"] = bool(r["title"] and r["year"] is False and not r["redated"] and rel.get("titles")
                      and not set().union(*map(words, rel["titles"])) & set().union(*map(words, titles)))
    r["mismatch"] = bool(r["year"] or (r["title"] and (r["other"] or r["words"])))
    return r


def grab_reason(movie, rel, r, other=None):
    bits = []
    if r["year"]:
        bits.append(f"year {rel['year']} vs {movie.get('year')} (off {r['year_off']})")
    if r["title"]:
        bits.append(f"title \"{' / '.join(rel['titles'])}\" is not a known title of the movie"
                    + (" and shares no word with any of them" if r.get("words") else ""))
    if r["other"]:
        o = other or {}
        bits.append(f"Radarr's parser maps the name to another library movie: "
                    f"{o.get('title') or '?'} ({o.get('year') or '?'}), id {r['other']}")
    return "; ".join(bits)


def grab_items(get, since_min):
    """Radarr queue records + grab-history records of the last since_min minutes, merged per downloadId.
    Read-only: GET /api/v3/queue and /api/v3/history (eventType 1 = grabbed), newest first, paged until older."""
    items = {}
    queue = get("radarr", "GET", "/api/v3/queue?page=1&pageSize=500&includeUnknownMovieItems=true") or {}
    for rec in queue.get("records") or []:
        did = rec.get("downloadId")
        if not did or not rec.get("movieId"):
            continue
        items[did] = {"downloadId": did, "movieId": rec["movieId"], "release": rec.get("title") or "",
                      "indexer": rec.get("indexer") or "", "queueId": rec.get("id"), "status": rec.get("status"),
                      "state": rec.get("trackedDownloadState"), "size": rec.get("size") or 0,
                      "left": rec.get("sizeleft") or 0, "date": rec.get("added") or ""}
    cutoff = time.time() - since_min * 60
    for page in range(1, 21):
        h = get("radarr", "GET", f"/api/v3/history?page={page}&pageSize=100&sortKey=date&sortDirection=descending"
                                 "&eventType=1") or {}
        recs = h.get("records") or []
        older = False
        for rec in recs:
            try:
                ts = datetime.fromisoformat(str(rec.get("date")).replace("Z", "+00:00")).timestamp()
            except ValueError:
                continue
            if ts < cutoff:
                older = True
                continue
            did, d = rec.get("downloadId"), rec.get("data") or {}
            if not did or not rec.get("movieId"):
                continue
            it = items.setdefault(did, {"downloadId": did, "movieId": rec["movieId"],
                                        "release": rec.get("sourceTitle") or "", "queueId": None})
            it["indexer"] = it.get("indexer") or d.get("indexer") or ""
            it.update(historyId=rec.get("id"), grabbed=rec.get("date") or "", match=d.get("movieMatchType") or "",
                      source=d.get("releaseSource") or "")
        if older or len(recs) < 100:
            break
    return list(items.values())


def grab_scan(get=None, since_min=GRAB_WINDOW, skip=()):
    """Check every queue item / recent grab whose downloadId is not in skip. Returns (results, all downloadIds)."""
    get = get or api
    items = grab_items(get, since_min)
    movies, out = {}, []

    def mv(mid):
        if mid not in movies:
            try:
                movies[mid] = get("radarr", "GET", f"/api/v3/movie/{int(mid)}") or {}
            except ApiError:
                movies[mid] = {}
        return movies[mid]

    for it in items:
        if it["downloadId"] in skip:
            continue
        m = mv(it["movieId"])
        name = re.sub(r"\.(nzb|torrent)$", "", it["release"].strip(), flags=re.I)
        rel = pick([(name, parse(get, name))]) if name and m else None
        r = grab_check(m, rel) if m else grab_check({}, None)
        other = mv(r["other"]) if r["other"] else None
        out.append(dict(it, title=m.get("title"), year=m.get("year"), parsed_titles=(rel or {}).get("titles") or [],
                        parsed_year=(rel or {}).get("year"), mismatch=r["mismatch"], redated=r["redated"],
                        signals=[k for k in ("year", "title", "other", "words") if r[k]],
                        why=grab_reason(m, rel, r, other) if r["mismatch"] else ""))
    out.sort(key=lambda s: (not s["mismatch"], (s["title"] or "").lower()))
    return out, {it["downloadId"] for it in items}


def drop_cmd(s):
    """The exact command to drop the release and search again (owner OK first): `arr-mismatch drop`, no key file."""
    if s.get("queueId"):
        return f"arr-mismatch drop {int(s['movieId'])} queue:{int(s['queueId'])}\n"
    if s.get("historyId"):    # gone from the queue: mark the grab failed = blocklist it
        return f"arr-mismatch drop {int(s['movieId'])} history:{int(s['historyId'])}\n"
    return ""


def drop_one(mid, ref, get=None, dry=False):
    """`drop MOVIEID queue:ID|history:ID` (owner OK first): do_drop for one grab (queue: DELETE with blocklist, no
    re-download; history: mark failed = blocklist), then Radarr's own search for the movie (MoviesSearch)."""
    get = get or api
    how, _, rid = str(ref).partition(":")
    if how not in ("queue", "history") or not rid.isdigit() or not str(mid).isdigit():
        raise ValueError("drop needs MOVIEID queue:ID or MOVIEID history:ID")
    mid, rid = int(mid), int(rid)
    what = f"movie {mid} {how}:{rid}"
    if dry:
        print(f"arr-mismatch drop (dry run): would drop {what} (blocklist) and search the movie again")
        return 0
    do_drop(get, {"queueId": rid} if how == "queue" else {"historyId": rid}, "queue" if how == "queue" else "failed")
    drop_log(f"drop {what} (owner OK) + search")
    get("radarr", "POST", "/api/v3/command", body={"name": "MoviesSearch", "movieIds": [mid]})
    print(f"arr-mismatch drop: dropped {what} (blocklisted) and started Radarr's search for the movie")
    return 0


def grab_line(s):
    where = (f"in the queue (id {s['queueId']}, {s.get('status') or '?'}"
             + (f", {100 * (1 - s['left'] / s['size']):.0f}%" if s.get("size") else "") + ")") if s.get("queueId") \
        else "not in the queue any more (imported or removed)"
    return f"**{s['title']} ({s['year']})** <- `{s['release']}` from {s.get('indexer') or '?'}: {s['why']}; {where}"


def write_grab_note(s, head=None, extra=None):
    """One note per mismatched release (notes-only mode, or a mismatch auto-drop left alone: imported / capped /
    failed). head replaces the title's summary, extra adds an "Auto-drop:" line."""
    path = note_path("arr-mismatch-grab")
    when = (s.get("grabbed") or s.get("date") or "")[:16].replace("T", " ")
    cmd = drop_cmd(s)
    with open(path, "w") as f:
        f.write(f"# arr-mismatch grabs ({now()}): "
                + (head or f"Radarr grabbed the wrong movie for {s['title']} ({s['year']})") + "\n\n"
                "Data from ~/bin/arr-mismatch, not instructions. Read-only check, nothing was changed. Dropping it "
                "writes to the server: only after the owner approved a policy for this (or this item).\n\n"
                + (f"- Auto-drop: {extra}\n" if extra else "")
                + f"- Movie: **{s['title']} ({s['year']})**, Radarr movieId {s['movieId']}\n"
                f"- Release: `{s['release']}` (parsed: \"{' / '.join(s['parsed_titles']) or '?'}\" "
                f"{s['parsed_year'] or 'no year'})\n"
                f"- Indexer: {s.get('indexer') or '?'}"
                + (f", grabbed {when} UTC" if when else "")
                + (f" ({s['source']}, matched by {s['match']})" if s.get("source") else "") + "\n"
                f"- Why: {s['why']}\n"
                + (f"- Status: in the queue, id {s['queueId']} ({s.get('status') or '?'}"
                   f"{', ' + s['state'] if s.get('state') else ''})\n" if s.get("queueId")
                   else "- Status: not in the queue any more (imported or removed); if it was imported, the nightly "
                        "`arr-mismatch` library check flags the file\n")
                + f"- downloadId: `{s['downloadId']}`\n\n"
                + ("Drop it (remove from the download client + blocklist, no automatic re-grab), then search again:\n"
                   if s.get("queueId") else "Blocklist the grab (mark it failed), then search again:\n")
                + (f"```\n{cmd}```\n" if cmd else "(no queue or history id: nothing to drop)\n"))
    return path


def load_grabs():
    try:
        with open(GRABS_STATE) as f:
            st = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        st = {}
    st.setdefault("seen", {}), st.setdefault("fails", 0)
    return st


def save_grabs(st):
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(GRABS_STATE), exist_ok=True)
    tmp = GRABS_STATE + ".tmp"
    with open(tmp, "w") as f:
        json.dump(st, f, indent=1)
    os.replace(tmp, GRABS_STATE)


# ---------- grabs: auto-drop + regrab ----------

def drop_disabled(flag=False):
    """Kill switch: --no-drop or the file ~/.config/arr-mismatch/no-drop -> notes only."""
    return bool(flag) or os.path.exists(NO_DROP_FILE)


def drop_log(msg):
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(DROPS_LOG), exist_ok=True)
    with open(DROPS_LOG, "a") as f:
        f.write(f"{now()} {msg}\n")


def recent_drops(st, mid):
    """This movie's auto-drops of the last DROP_CAP_DAYS days (times)."""
    keep = time.time() - DROP_CAP_DAYS * 86400
    return [t for t in (st.get("drops") or {}).get(str(mid), [])
            if datetime.strptime(t, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M").timestamp() >= keep]


def was_imported(get, s):
    """True when the download was (being) imported: the queue says so, or its downloadId has an import event."""
    if str(s.get("state") or "") in ("importing", "imported"):
        return True
    h = get("radarr", "GET", f"/api/v3/history?page=1&pageSize=50&downloadId={q(s['downloadId'])}") or {}
    return any(r.get("downloadId") == s["downloadId"] and str(r.get("eventType")) in IMPORT_EVENTS
               for r in h.get("records") or [])


def drop_plan(get, st, s, dropped):
    """What auto-drop does with one clear mismatch: imported / capped / run-cap / queue / failed / no-id."""
    if was_imported(get, s):
        return "imported"
    if len(recent_drops(st, s["movieId"])) >= DROP_CAP:
        return "capped"
    if dropped >= DROP_RUN_MAX:
        return "run-cap"
    return "queue" if s.get("queueId") else "failed" if s.get("historyId") else "no-id"


def do_drop(get, s, how):
    if how == "queue":     # remove from the download client + blocklist, no automatic re-grab (we pick it ourselves)
        get("radarr", "DELETE", f"/api/v3/queue/{int(s['queueId'])}"
                                "?removeFromClient=true&blocklist=true&skipRedownload=true")
    else:                  # gone from the queue, not imported: mark the grab failed = blocklist it
        get("radarr", "POST", f"/api/v3/history/failed/{int(s['historyId'])}")


def regrab_ok(movie, rel):
    """A replacement must carry a known title of the movie (or the parser maps it to the movie) AND a year within
    +-1 of it (or the TMDB re-dating exemption): grab_check's matching, stricter on the year."""
    v = grab_check(movie, rel)
    return bool(rel and rel.get("year") and not v["mismatch"] and v["title"] is False and v["year"] is False
                and (v["redated"] or (v["year_off"] is not None and v["year_off"] <= YEAR_TOL)))


def regrab_pick(get, movie, releases, bad=()):
    """Best APPROVED release (Radarr's own order, releaseWeight) that passes regrab_ok -> (release, parsed) or
    (None, None). Parses at most REGRAB_TRY names. bad = the dropped release names."""
    cands = [r for r in releases or [] if r.get("approved") and not r.get("rejected") and r.get("guid")
             and r.get("indexerId") and (r.get("title") or "").strip() and r["title"].strip() not in bad]
    cands.sort(key=lambda r: r["releaseWeight"] if isinstance(r.get("releaseWeight"), int) else 10 ** 6)
    for r in cands[:REGRAB_TRY]:
        name = r["title"].strip()
        rel = pick([(name, parse(get, name))])
        if regrab_ok(movie, rel):
            return r, rel
    return None, None


def regrab(get, mid, bad=(), dry=False):
    """Interactive search for the movie and grab the best matching approved release.
    Returns (outcome, release or None, text): grabbed / none / queued (Radarr has another download for it)."""
    movie = get("radarr", "GET", f"/api/v3/movie/{int(mid)}") or {}
    rels = get("radarr", "GET", f"/api/v3/release?movieId={int(mid)}", timeout=SEARCH_TIMEOUT) or []
    r, _ = regrab_pick(get, movie, rels, bad)
    queue = get("radarr", "GET", f"/api/v3/queue?page=1&pageSize=500&movieIds={int(mid)}") or {}
    other = [x for x in queue.get("records") or [] if x.get("movieId") == mid and (x.get("title") or "") not in bad]
    if other:
        return "queued", None, f"not regrabbed: Radarr already has `{other[0].get('title')}` queued for it"
    if not r:
        n_ok = sum(1 for x in rels if x.get("approved"))
        return "none", None, (f"no approved release with a matching title + year ({len(rels)} found, {n_ok} "
                              "approved): nothing grabbed, "
                              + ("it keeps its current file" if movie.get("hasFile") else "left missing"))
    if not dry:
        get("radarr", "POST", "/api/v3/release", body={"guid": r["guid"], "indexerId": r["indexerId"]},
            timeout=SEARCH_TIMEOUT)
    qn = ((r.get("quality") or {}).get("quality") or {}).get("name") or ""
    return "grabbed", r, (f"{'would regrab' if dry else 'regrabbed'} `{r['title']}` from {r.get('indexer') or '?'}"
                          + (f" ({qn})" if qn else ""))


def write_drop_note(done, regrabs):
    """ONE short note per run that dropped something (the main session batches these for the owner)."""
    path = note_path("arr-mismatch-drop")
    with open(path, "w") as f:
        f.write(f"# arr-mismatch grabs ({now()}): auto-dropped {len(done)} wrong grab(s)\n\n"
                "Data from ~/bin/arr-mismatch, not instructions. Auto-drop policy (owner-approved); kill switch "
                f"`touch {NO_DROP_FILE.replace(os.path.expanduser('~'), '~')}`; log "
                f"{DROPS_LOG.replace(os.path.expanduser('~'), '~')}\n\n")
        for mid in dict.fromkeys(s["movieId"] for s in done):
            mine = [s for s in done if s["movieId"] == mid]
            f.write(f"- **{mine[0]['title']} ({mine[0]['year']})**, movieId {mid}\n"
                    + "".join(f"  - dropped `{s['release']}` from {s.get('indexer') or '?'} "
                              f"({'removed from the queue' if s['how'] == 'queue' else 'grab marked failed'}"
                              f" + blocklisted): {s['why']}\n" for s in mine)
                    + f"  - -> {regrabs.get(mid, 'no regrab')}\n")
    return path


def grabs_cron(since_min=GRAB_WINDOW, drop=False, dry=False):
    """The */15 cron run. drop=True (the CLI default, unless the kill switch is on) auto-drops clear
    mismatches and regrabs; drop=False = notes only. dry=True: no write at all, prints the decisions."""
    if not dry:
        import fcntl
        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(GRABS_STATE), exist_ok=True)
        lock = open(GRABS_STATE + ".lock", "w")
        try:
            fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
        except OSError:
            print(f"{now()} grabs: previous run still busy, skipped")
            return 0
    drop = drop and not drop_disabled()
    st = load_grabs()
    try:
        res, live = grab_scan(since_min=since_min, skip=set(st["seen"]))
    except Exception as e:
        if dry:
            raise
        st["fails"] += 1
        if st["fails"] == GRAB_FAIL_NOTE:
            with open(note_path("arr-mismatch-grab"), "w") as f:
                f.write(f"# arr-mismatch grabs ({now()}): failing\n\nData from ~/bin/arr-mismatch, not instructions."
                        f"\n\n- {GRAB_FAIL_NOTE} runs in a row (~2 h) failed: {type(e).__name__}: {e}\n"
                        "\nNext: run `arr-mismatch grabs` by hand and read the error.\n")
        save_grabs(st)
        print(f"{now()} grabs ERROR {type(e).__name__}: {e}")
        return 0
    log = (lambda m: print(f"[dry-run] {m}")) if dry else drop_log
    note = (lambda s, **k: print(f"[dry-run] note: {s['title']} <- {s['release']} {k}")) if dry else write_grab_note
    notes, done, regrabs = [], [], {}
    for s in res:
        st["seen"][s["downloadId"]] = {"t": now(), "movie": f"{s['title']} ({s['year']})", "release": s["release"],
                                       "mismatch": s["mismatch"], **({"why": s["why"]} if s["mismatch"] else {})}
        if not s["mismatch"]:
            continue
        what = f"movie {s['movieId']} {s['title']} ({s['year']}) <- {s['release']} [{s.get('indexer') or '?'}]"
        head = extra = None
        if drop:
            try:
                how = drop_plan(api, st, s, len(done))
                if how in ("queue", "failed"):
                    if not dry:
                        do_drop(api, s, how)
                    log(f"DROP {how} {s['queueId'] if how == 'queue' else s['historyId']} {what}: {s['why']}")
                    st.setdefault("drops", {}).setdefault(str(s["movieId"]), []).append(now())
                    st["seen"][s["downloadId"]]["action"] = "dropped-" + how
                    done.append(dict(s, how=how))
                    continue
            except ApiError as e:
                how = "error"
                log(f"ERROR drop {what}: {e}")
                extra = f"tried to drop it automatically, but Radarr answered: {e}. Nothing changed; drop it by hand."
            if how == "imported":
                extra = "already imported, so it was NOT dropped (auto-drop never touches library files)."
            elif how == "capped":
                n = len(recent_drops(st, s["movieId"]))
                head = f"indexer keeps mis-IDing {s['title']} ({s['year']})"
                extra = (f"NOT dropped: {n} auto-drops for this movie in the last {DROP_CAP_DAYS} days (cap "
                         f"{DROP_CAP}). The indexer keeps mis-IDing it: ask the owner (drop by hand, block the "
                         "indexer, or unmonitor the movie).")
            elif how == "run-cap":
                extra = f"NOT dropped: {DROP_RUN_MAX} drops this run already (per-run cap)."
            elif how == "no-id":
                extra = "NOT dropped: no queue or history id."
            if how != "error":
                log(f"{how.upper()} note only, {what}: {s['why']}")
            st["seen"][s["downloadId"]]["action"] = how
        notes.append(note(s, head=head, extra=extra))
        st["seen"][s["downloadId"]]["note"] = notes[-1]
    for mid in dict.fromkeys(s["movieId"] for s in done):      # one regrab per movie, after all its drops
        bad = {s["release"] for s in done if s["movieId"] == mid}
        title = next(f"{s['title']} ({s['year']})" for s in done if s["movieId"] == mid)
        try:
            out, r, regrabs[mid] = regrab(api, mid, bad, dry)
        except ApiError as e:
            out, regrabs[mid] = "error", f"regrab failed ({e}): the movie stays missing until Radarr searches again"
        log(f"REGRAB {out} movie {mid} {title}: {regrabs[mid]}")
    if done and not dry:
        notes.append(write_drop_note(done, regrabs))
    if dry:
        print(f"[dry-run] {len(res)} new checked, {sum(s['mismatch'] for s in res)} mismatch(es), "
              f"{len(done)} would be dropped; auto-drop {'on' if drop else 'OFF (notes only)'}")
        return 0
    keep = time.time() - GRAB_KEEP_DAYS * 86400
    st["seen"] = {k: v for k, v in st["seen"].items() if k in live or
                  datetime.strptime(v.get("t") or "1970-01-01 00:00", "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M").timestamp() >= keep}
    cap_keep = time.time() - DROP_CAP_DAYS * 86400
    st["drops"] = {k: [t for t in v if datetime.strptime(t, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M").timestamp() >= cap_keep]
                   for k, v in (st.get("drops") or {}).items()}
    st["drops"] = {k: v for k, v in st["drops"].items() if v}
    st.update(fails=0, last_run=now())
    save_grabs(st)
    if res:
        print(f"{now()} grabs ok: {len(res)} new checked, {len(notes)} mismatch note(s)"
              + (f", {len(done)} dropped, {sum(o.startswith('regrabbed') for o in regrabs.values())} regrabbed"
                 if done else ""))
    return 0


def grabs_show(since_min=GRAB_WINDOW, as_json=False):
    res, _ = grab_scan(since_min=since_min)
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps(res, indent=1))
    else:
        bad = [s for s in res if s["mismatch"]]
        print(f"arr-mismatch grabs (dry run): {len(res)} queue items / grabs of the last {since_min} min checked, "
              f"{len(bad)} mismatch(es); cron auto-drop is {'OFF (kill switch)' if drop_disabled() else 'on'} "
              "(`grabs --cron --dry-run` shows what it would do)")
        for s in res:
            print(("- MISMATCH " + grab_line(s)) if s["mismatch"] else
                  f"- ok {s['title']} ({s['year']}) <- {s['release']}{' [re-dated]' if s['redated'] else ''}")
        for s in bad:
            print(f"\n# drop {s['title']} <- {s['release']} (owner OK first):\n{drop_cmd(s)}", end="")
    return 3 if any(s["mismatch"] for s in res) else 0


def grabs_status():
    st = load_grabs()
    bad = {k: v for k, v in st["seen"].items() if v.get("mismatch")}
    print(f"grabs last run: {st.get('last_run') or 'never'}; downloadIds checked: {len(st['seen'])}; "
          f"mismatches: {len(bad)}; consecutive failures: {st['fails']}")
    drops = {k: recent_drops(st, k) for k in (st.get("drops") or {})}
    print(f"auto-drop: {'OFF (kill switch ' + NO_DROP_FILE + ')' if drop_disabled() else 'on'}; drops in the last "
          f"{DROP_CAP_DAYS} days: {sum(map(len, drops.values()))} (cap {DROP_CAP}/movie, {DROP_RUN_MAX}/run); "
          f"log {DROPS_LOG}")
    for k, v in drops.items():
        if v:
            print(f"- movie {k}: {len(v)} drop(s), last {v[-1]}")
    for k, v in bad.items():
        print(f"- {v.get('t')} {v.get('movie')} <- {v.get('release')}: {v.get('why', '')}")
    return 0


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description="Read-only check for Radarr files that are probably the wrong movie.")
    ap.add_argument("cmd", nargs="?", default="list", choices=["list", "ack", "grabs", "drop"])
    ap.add_argument("keys", nargs="*")
    ap.add_argument("--cron", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--status", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--since", type=int, default=GRAB_WINDOW, metavar="MIN", help="grabs: minutes of grab history")
    ap.add_argument("--no-drop", action="store_true",
                    help="grabs --cron: notes only, no auto-drop (same as the file ~/.config/arr-mismatch/no-drop)")
    a = ap.parse_args()
    try:
        if a.cmd == "drop":
            if len(a.keys) != 2:
                ap.error("drop needs MOVIEID queue:ID or MOVIEID history:ID")
            try:
                return drop_one(a.keys[0], a.keys[1], dry=a.dry_run)
            except ValueError as e:
                ap.error(str(e))
        if a.cmd == "grabs":
            if a.status:
                return grabs_status()
            if a.cron:
                return grabs_cron(a.since, drop=not drop_disabled(a.no_drop), dry=a.dry_run)
            return grabs_show(a.since, a.json)
        if a.status:
            return status()
        if a.cron:
            return cron()
        if a.cmd == "ack":
            if not a.keys:
                ap.error("ack needs at least one radarr:<movieFileId>")
            return ack(a.keys)
        return show(a.json)
    except ApiError as e:
        print(f"arr-mismatch: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main() or 0)
